# Keep the build context small.
#
# The Dockerfile copies only what it names, so nothing here could reach the
# image anyway. What this prevents is the whole directory being handed to the
# daemon first: on a machine that has run the tests, that means node_modules, a
# PouchDB replica and a set of SQLite stores, which is hundreds of megabytes
# sent over a socket to be thrown away. It costs nothing in CI, where the
# checkout is clean, and a great deal when building locally from the `build:`
# fallback in the compose file.
#
# Anything holding real vault data is also listed, so no future COPY can pick
# one up by accident.

node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.git/
.github/

# Scratch and derived data, some of which is a copy of the vault.
/tmp/
/data/
/fixtures/private/
*.sqlite
*.log

# Never in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store
